               <msContents>
                  <summary>The quires are not attached to the spine.</summary>
                  <msItem xml:id="ms_i0">
                     <locus from="1r" to="114v">1r-114v</locus>
                     <textLang xml:lang="ar">Arabic</textLang>
                     <title ref="LIT0049IHA" type="acephalous apodous"/>
                     <incipit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#1r">-1r</locus>أو إثما ثم يرم به بريئا فقد احتمل بهتانا وإثما مبينا <note>Verse 4:112.</note>
                     </incipit>
                     <explicit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#114v">-114v</locus>وتسلموا على اهلها ذلكم خير لكم لعلكم تذكرون , فان لم تجدوا فيها احدا \ فلا  <note>Verse 24:27-28. The last word is the catchword.</note>
                     </explicit>
                     <note>The order of the folios is disrupted. A continuous section written in one hand, containing verses 4:112-24:28 is on folios 1r-63v, 66r-75v, 86r-114v. Folios 64r-65v are also written by the same hand, but contain verses from Sūras 35 and 36. Folios 76r-85v are written in a different hand and the text is placed within a frame. They contain the verses 4:123-5:44.</note>
                     <note/>
                  </msItem>
